### Crypto Pivot: NSec.Cryptography / X25519 → Built-in P-256

The master plan and earlier tracker entries specified "ECDH X25519 via NSec.Cryptography 22.4.0". During
implementation, repeated integration problems with the NSec package prevented a stable build. The
decision was made to use the built-in .NET System.Security.Cryptography.ECDiffieHellman with the NIST
P-256 curve instead. P-256 is well-reviewed, meets the same security bar as X25519 for this use case,
requires no third-party dependency, and is natively available in .NET 7+. The session key derivation
uses HKDF-SHA256 over the raw ECDH secret, salted with the certificate SPKI hash and with info tag
"remex-pair-v1" — identical to the originally specified design except for the curve choice.
NSec.Cryptography does not appear in any .csproj file. All prior tracker entries referencing X25519/NSec
should be read as P-256/built-in .NET.

