## Audit Remediation — 2026-05-09

All blockers and high/medium/low items from the 2026-05-09 pre-polish audit report have been resolved.

| Item | Severity | Status | Resolution |
|---|---|---|---|
| BLOCKER-1: No pairing gate on WebSocket commands | CRITICAL | ✅ RESOLVED | Per-connection isPaired flag in PingPongHandler.HandleAsync; RequiresPairing() helper gates all non-handshake message types. |
| BLOCKER-2: AcceptSelfSignedCertificate returns true on unknown cert | CRITICAL | ✅ RESOLVED | ConnectionViewModel now rejects unknown SPKI hashes; pre-loads pin snapshot synchronously before TLS callback; trust-on-first-use only when explicitly permitted. |
| BLOCKER-3: Five unauthorized tile services | CRITICAL | ✅ RESOLVED | Scope expansion authorized by user; tracker updated to reflect 8-tile scope with unlockAndRun on all. |
| BLOCKER-4: No unlockAndRun on tile services | CRITICAL | ✅ RESOLVED | All 8 tile services now use unlockAndRun {}. Lock, MonitorOff, RestartUefi, WakeOnLan updated 2026-05-09. |
| HIGH-1: NSec/X25519 tracker mismatch | HIGH | ✅ RESOLVED | Tracker updated to document P-256 via built-in .NET ECDiffieHellman. See crypto pivot note in Phase 1. |
| HIGH-2: PairingService singleton concurrent session corruption | HIGH | ✅ RESOLVED | StartPairingAsync now rejects concurrent requests immediately (semaphore try-acquire with WaitAsync(0)). Single-active-session semantics enforced with clear error message. |
| HIGH-3: Plaintext TCP fallback on cert load failure | HIGH | ✅ RESOLVED | RemexNetworkListener.StartListeningAsync now throws InvalidOperationException on cert load failure; per-connection null-cert fallback path also returns rather than accepting plaintext. |
| HIGH-4: CorrelationId not set on outgoing commands | HIGH | ✅ RESOLVED | RemexNativeClient.SendCommandAsync now sets CorrelationId = id on outgoing message. HandleMessage now looks up by CorrelationId first, falls back to first-pending for legacy hosts. |
| HIGH-5: Android 17 ACCESS_LOCAL_NETWORK runtime permission | HIGH | ✅ RESOLVED | ConnectionScreen.kt requests permission at connect/discover time; denial surfaces rationale snackbar; strings added; guarded on SDK_INT >= 37. See 2D-android17-lan track. |
| MED-1: HostBootstrapper double-instantiates CertificateService | MEDIUM | ✅ RESOLVED | Removed first AddSingleton<ICertificateService, CertificateService>() registration; single manual instantiation with AddSingleton(instance) remains. One object, one DI registration. |
| MED-2: PingPongHandler never validates ProtocolVersion | MEDIUM | ✅ RESOLVED | Messages with ProtocolVersion < 2 receive a CommandResponse error and break out of the receive loop. |
| MED-3: ic_hibernate.xml wrong icon (login arrow) | MEDIUM | ✅ RESOLVED | Replaced with a bed + crescent moon vector path appropriate for hibernate. |
| MED-4: StreamDownloadAsync fire-and-forget | MEDIUM | ✅ RESOLVED | Wrapped in Task.Run with try/catch; errors logged and surfaced to client via FileTransferEnd error response. |
| MED-5: FileTransferService bare catch{} | MEDIUM | ✅ RESOLVED | Replaced with catch(Exception ex) + _logger.LogError(); ILogger<FileTransferService> injected via constructor. |
| LOW-1: PinnedCertStore.EnsureLoaded() uses _lock.Wait() | LOW | N/A — ALREADY CORRECT | EnsureLoadedAsync() already uses await _lock.WaitAsync(). Sync EnsureLoaded() uses _lock.Wait() which is correct for the sync TLS callback caller. No change needed. |
| LOW-2: RemexNativeClient.Dispose() blocks on async | LOW | ✅ RESOLVED | Implemented IAsyncDisposable.DisposeAsync(); Dispose() forwards to fire-and-forget Task.Run to avoid blocking the caller. |
| LOW-3: allowBackup="true" undocumented | LOW | ✅ RESOLVED | Comment added to AndroidManifest.xml explaining the safety properties (data_extraction_rules exclusions + non-exportable Keystore master key) and warning future maintainers. |

