| 2026-05-08 | 2A | HIGH | Android upload from phone hung indefinitely on "Preparing transfer…" notification when the source content URI did not expose OpenableColumns.SIZE (Drive, Photos, Recents). Notification was indeterminate forever even though chunks were flowing. | RESOLVED: queryMetadata now falls back to AssetFileDescriptor.length, handleProgress + showTransferProgress render bytes-only progress when total is unknown so the UI shows live activity instead of a stuck "Preparing" string |
| 2026-05-08 | 2A | HIGH | RemexNativeClient.SendMessageAsync was not thread-safe — outbound queue serialized chunks, but SendCommandAsync called SendMessageAsync directly. A command racing a chunk flood could throw "There is already one outstanding 'SendAsync'" and tank the upload. | RESOLVED: added a SemaphoreSlim send gate around _webSocket.SendAsync so all paths into the WebSocket are serialized |
| 2026-05-08 | 2A | MEDIUM | FileTransferService only enforced MaxUploadBytes on start.TotalBytes. Mobile clients legitimately send 0 when the URI lacks SIZE, so a buggy/hostile peer could stream past the cap. | RESOLVED: FileTransferHandler.HandleFileTransferChunkAsync now enforces a running 5 GB cap on uploads, aborts the transfer, deletes the partial file, and acks failure |
